# Renders are reproducible from the seed, the script and the app, so the
# intermediates are not worth versioning — the raw Playwright capture alone is
# ~30MB per run, and it changes on every render.
#
# What IS committed is the finished deliverable MINUS the video itself: the
# subtitles, the YouTube text and the timing manifest — about 1MB for the whole
# library, and enough to say what was made and when.
#
# ⚠️ The mp4s used to be committed too, for the same reason ("anybody can watch
# it without running anything"). Sixty-eight of them came to 719MB — two thirds
# of a git repository that every clone, every CI checkout and the bundle-over-
# SSH prod deploy has to carry, forever, because git history is not editable in
# passing. A render is reproducible from the seed, the script and the app; a
# finished video belongs wherever finished videos are published, not here.
*
!.gitignore
!*/
*/*
!*/*.srt
!*/*.youtube.txt
!*/*.timeline.json
